D = {
 "Luthic|VGM": "Orc mother goddess and wife of Gruumsh. She holds the tribe together while his rage drives it outward. Her followers guard the dens, raise the young, and craft weapons, armor, and tools. They keep cave bears as guardians, grow their claws long, and use ritual, omens, and fear to keep order.",
 "Majere|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of meditation and discipline. He is remote and quiet. His monks live in contemplative monasteries, which also raise many orphans. Those who leave the cloister often take Majere as a surname.",
 "Malar|FRHOF": "Bestial god of the hunt, bloodshed, and savage predators. He answers no prayers for mercy. His followers imitate his hunting skill, wear trophies from slain beasts, and must prove themselves in combat before joining the priesthood. A secret High Hunt makes a chosen victim the prey for a day and a night.",
 "Malyk|MTF": "Drow god of rebellion and chaos, linked to wild mages whose power seems random. Lolth's faithful try to stamp out his worship, yet some pray to him in secret. Outcast and low-ranked drow sacrifice to him quietly, and discovered wild mages are usually killed or driven out.",
 "Mask|FRHOF": "Trickster god of thieves, spies, and everything done in shadow. People whisper to him when stealth or intrigue is needed. Commoners carry a cheap pouch of coin called Mask's purse, which thieves treat as a gift. His priests, the demarches, run the local underworld in veil-masks.",
 "Melora|EGW": "Exandrian goddess of wild nature, seas, and untamed lands. Hunters, elves, and sailors seek her guidance, and she wanders the planes hunting things that corrupt the wilds. Her faith commands protecting wilderness, destroying abominations of nature, and respecting the natural order. Her holy day is Wild's Grandeur at the vernal equinox.",
 "Merrshaulk|VGM": "Yuan-ti god who sleeps in a deep slumber, mirroring his people's long hiding. He still grants spells to clergy, and waking him takes many ritual murders. Pit masters, malison warlocks, lead his worship and believe he will soon awaken, shed his skin, and return the yuan-ti to power.",
 "Mielikki|FRHOF": "Loyal, good-natured goddess of forests and rangers. Her followers gather in wooded glades and carve shrines into dead trunks, marking places where no one may cut or hunt. Her priests protect forest life and wear seasonal leaf capes. On Greengrass and Midsummer, she grants the Wild Ride on unicorns.",
 "Milil|FRHOF": "God of poetry, song, and inspiration, often called Oghma's left hand. Bards, minstrels, and anyone about to perform pray to him. His followers tend toward hedonism, and tuneservants travel with adventurers to write ballads. On Midsummer, his priests hold the Grand Revel, a satirical festival that tyrants ban.",
 "Mishakal|DSOTDQ": "Krynn goddess of compassion, healing, and love. Healers and community guardians worship her. She has reached out to chosen heroes through history to ease suffering, and her faithful offer healing and comfort to everyone, even enemies.",
 "Mogis|MOT": "Theran god of slaughter, violence, and war, and the brother and rival of Iroas. He delights in cruelty and the humiliation of the beaten, trading decency and mercy for rage. The vengeful call on him, soldiers dread his bloodlust, and he wants to see the world burn so only the brutal survive.",
 "Moradin|EGW": "Exandrian dwarf god, patron of smiths, miners, and artisans, who shaped the mountains and protects home and family. Temples mark the center of dwarven strongholds. His faith asks for stoic resilience, loyalty to family, clan, and people, and a lasting legacy. His holy day is Deep Solace, spent in meditation on family.",
 "Moradin|MTF": "Dwarf father god who forged his children from metal and gems and gave them souls. He is master of every dwarven craft and patron of artisans. His priests judge the quality of a stronghold's work, keep books of techniques, and assess young dwarves to decide their callings. Their decisions go unquestioned.",
 "Morgion|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of disease and decay. He is solitary and secretive, ignoring the other gods and brooding in his Bronze Tower. His worshipers copy him by meeting in the dark and keeping everything secret.",
 "Myrkul|FRHOF": "Cold god of death, decay, and old age, one of the Dead Three. He binds slain souls into wax skulls to drain their knowledge. People dread him more than they pray to him. His followers are morose necromancers and undertakers, with shrines at burial grounds and rare temples ringed by vast catacombs.",
 "Mystra|FRHOF": "Goddess of magic and the Weave, widely worshiped wherever spells are used. Her faithful spread and preserve magic and help gifted people find mentors. Dweomerkeepers serve her temples, the Knights of the Mystic Fire are her martial champions, and her Chosen wield silver fire.",
 "Naviask|EGW": "A former balor turned fey spirit by Titania, now devoted to healing scarred land. He wanders the wastes of Xhorhas, glimpsed only by those he chooses, and shares power with people of similar heart. He keeps a balor's shape softened by flowers and vines, with sunlight in place of inner fire and a radiant whip.",
 "Nebelun|MTF": "Gnome god of invention and discovery, called the Meddler. She is fearless and her plans rarely go right, yet her mistakes often yield brilliant breakthroughs. All gnomes see her as the spirit of tinkering, crediting lucky accidents to her. Garl and the pantheon must keep her on task.",
 "Nuitari|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of evil magic and darkness, patron of the Black Robes and other wicked mages. He encourages selfish, destructive spellcasting. His power flows through the black moon that bears his name, visible only by the stars it hides.",
 "Nylea|MOT": "Wild, carefree Theran goddess of the hunt, forests, seasons, and rebirth. Hunters pray to her for success, and she is the world's finest archer. She punishes poachers and wanton killers, sometimes holds back the seasons in anger, and her priests often serve as midwives.",
 "Oghma|FRHOF": "God of knowledge, thought, and ideas, shown by a blank scroll. He answers threats to learning slowly, after consulting Deneir, Milil, and Gond. Sages, students, and teachers worship him. His temples double as public libraries, hold a nightly Covenant reading, and fund themselves by selling maps and scrolls.",
 "Olladra|ERLW": "Eberron Sovereign of Feast and Fortune. She gives joy and grants luck, and she is patron to entertainers, gamblers, and anyone willing to take a chance.",
 "Onatar|ERLW": "Eberron Sovereign of Fire and Forge. He guides common smiths and artificers alike and inspires anyone who makes something new.",
 "Paladine|DSOTDQ": "Krynn Father of Good and the Platinum Dragon, known as Bahamut elsewhere. He leads the good gods and favors order, justice, and mercy. He teaches that fair laws hold society together, and his clerics help write and uphold them. He sometimes walks Krynn as the befuddled mage Fizban.",
 "Pelor|EGW": "Exandrian sun god, lord of summer, farming, and time. Farmers and common folk worship him, and he patrons paladins, rangers, and those who hunt aberrations. His creed is to watch for evil, ease the suffering of the innocent, and bring light with mercy. His holy day is Highsummer.",
 "Pharika|MOT": "Theran goddess of affliction, medicine, alchemy, and aging. She hid secrets of healing and poison across the world and treats mortals as test subjects. Her cures work but cost pain or years of life. Alchemists and the sick pray to her, and she is cunning and watchful.",
 "Phenax|MOT": "Masked Theran god of lies, cheats, gambling, and betrayal, and the opposite of Heliod. A former mortal who escaped the Underworld, he is a perfect actor who tempts champions of law into small compromises until they fall. He wants no throne, only to disrupt his fellow gods.",
 "Procan|GOS": "Chaotic neutral god of the sea and weather who offers the Tempest domain. He is as sudden as a storm at sea and holds every treasure lost beneath the waves. Sailors throw food, drink, or treasure overboard as offerings, and he curses those who loot wrecks without his clerics' blessing.",
 "Purphoros|MOT": "Theran god of the forge, volcanic earth, and fire, and of artisans and obsession. He is impulsive and mercurial, endlessly crafting and then destroying his works. He inspires all creation, and his followers brought bronze to Theros and now work iron. His wrath melts stars and shakes the land.",
 "Quajath|EGW": "A fragment of a vast worm creature tied to Torog, entombed beneath the ice of Eiselcross. Wormkin who fed on its regrowing flesh act as its vessels. They offer broken minds purpose, raw magic, and fractured secrets, and hope to free the Undermaw one day.",
 "Raei|EGW": "Exandrian goddess of atonement and compassion who believes the corrupt can be redeemed. The Lord of the Nine Hells betrayed her trust, and her faith faded until recently. Rural healers and philosophers follow her creed of mercy and fellowship, with swift justice only for the remorselessly evil.",
 "Reorx|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of creation, inspiration, and craft, said to have made gnomes, dwarves, kender, and Krynn itself. He invents things that change the world and push its people to act.",
 "Rillifane Rallathil|MTF": "Elf god of forests, seasons, and beasts, who takes the form of a gigantic oak whose roots touch every plant. His mostly druid followers are insular and secretive. They leave offerings of animal carvings, golden acorns, and holly at ancient trees, and they debate whether the great oak is literal or symbolic.",
 "Sargonnas|DSOTDQ": "Krynn god of flame, vengeance, and wrath, shown as a monstrous minotaur. He is Takhisis's consort, yet he schemes against her as often as he serves her. Those who seek retribution worship him, and many minotaurs know him as Sargas.",
 "Savras|SCAG": "God of divination and fortunetelling with few worshipers but many casual prayers, such as rhymes to glimpse a future spouse. He has no active temples, only shrines hidden in libraries. Investigators, diviners, and judges honor him with decorated staffs, recalling the legend that he was once trapped in Azuth's staff.",
 "Segojan Earthcaller|MTF": "Gnome god seen as a kind, modest hero and the best cook among the gods. He heals any sickness through his knowledge of underground plants and creatures and can burrow through anything. Gnomes revere him as a healer and hearth protector, and as a guide for souls whose bodies are buried before worms take them.",
 "Sehanine|EGW": "Exandrian goddess of moonlight, autumn, illusion, and love, widely worshiped by elves and halflings. She shelters lovers with shadows, and people who work in darkness ask her blessing. Her creed urges pursuing your passions and avoiding both fanatical light and total darkness. Elves celebrate her at the decade's biggest full moon.",
 "Sehanine Moonbow|MTF": "Elf goddess of the moon, mysteries, and cycles of life and death. She is Corellon's companion and calming influence. She aids elf births, greets the dying, and patrons the lost, travelers, and seekers of meaning. Elves ask her for relief from madness, and her priests read dreams for guidance.",
 "Selvetarm|MTF": "Drow champion of Lolth and patron of warriors, shown with eight arms. Lolth keeps him bound in webs, freeing him only in dire need. Tricked into absorbing a demon's evil power, he became a berserk engine of slaughter. Low-caste drow warriors pray to him for battle prowess.",
 "Selûne|FRHOF": "Ancient Faerûn goddess of the moon, stars, navigation, and motherhood. Many see the moon as her literal gaze and the lights trailing it as her tears, and she is the rival of her sister Shar. Sailors, night workers, and the lost pray to her. The Swords of the Lady are her jovial, improvising knights.",
 "Shar|FRHOF": "Goddess of darkness, night, secrets, loss, and forgetfulness, the dark twin of Selûne. Those in pain pray to her to forget it. Her priests nurture their own wounds, and realms often ban her worship, which pushes the faith into secrecy and revenge. The Order of the Dark Moon trains her stealthy agents.",
 "Shargaas|VGM": "Orc god of darkness and the unknown, murderous and secretive. His cultists live apart in the deepest lair or pose as warriors. They cull weak orcs in secret, a taboo subject, and sell assassination, theft, and kidnapping services to war chiefs, even though Gruumsh dislikes subterfuge.",
 "Shaundakul|FRHOF": "God of travel, travelers, and portals. His worship has faded since the fall of Myth Drannor, where his chief temple stands. A few priests wear a trailing glove and protect old stone shrines. Each shrine links to another and opens a wind portal when its command word is spoken.",
 "Sheela Peryroyl|MTF": "Halfling goddess of nature, farming, and weather who merged her spirit with plants and trees to provide for her kin. Every village keeps a grove, patch, or flower bed for offerings, ideally tended by a druid. Halflings apologize to her for stepping on flowers and ask her leave before felling a tree.",
 "Shinare|DSOTDQ": "Krynn goddess of wealth, industry, and commerce. Merchants follow her, and thieves sometimes do too, since she covers fair and crooked trade alike. Most see her as a goddess of fair dealing, and people pray for her favor while bargaining.",
}
